                        Solution
 1-Login to jenkins UI with:
    username admin
    password Admin321
 2-Ensure the following plugins are installed:
  Go to Manage Jenkins > plugins > Available Plugins > Search thw following and install:
   .Publish Over SSH
   .SSH Credentials
  After installation, restart Jenkins and refresh the UI if it gets stuck.
 3-Add Credentials
  Navigate to Manage Jenkins → Credentials → Global → System → Add credentials.
 Add SSH credentials for:
   .App Server 1 (stapp01) → user: kodekloud_roy, password: asdfgdsd.
   .Storage Server (ststor01) → user: natasha, password: (use the provided storage server password).
 4-Go to Manage Jenkins > System > Add SSH servers > Apply:
   .Go to Manage Jenkins → System → SSH Sites.
   .Add entries for stapp01 and ststor01 with their respective credentials.
    For each click on Advance > click on User password authentification or use a different key > Go to password and enter the correct password.
 5-Create the Job
   .From Jenkins dashboard → New Item → Enter name: database-backup → Select Freestyle project → Click OK.
 6-Configure Build Trigger
   .Go to Build Triggers → Check Build periodically.
  Enter cron expression:
   */10 * * * *
    (runs every 10 minutes).
   .Add build step > Send files or execute commands over ssh > add this lines in execute command:

 #!/bin/bash

# Create temporary backup directory
mkdir -p /tmp/db-backup

# Take MySQL dump of kodekloud_db01
mysqldump -u kodekloud_roy -p'asdfgdsd' kodekloud_db01 > /tmp/db-backup/db_$(date +%F).sql

# Install sshpass if missing
if ! command -v sshpass >/dev/null 2>&1; then
  sudo yum install -y sshpass || sudo apt-get install -y sshpass
fi

# Copy dump to storage server (replace ACTUAL_PASSWORD with natasha's real password)
sshpass -p 'ACTUAL_PASSWORD' scp -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no /tmp/db-backup/*.sql natasha@ststor01:/home/natasha/db_backups/

# Clean up
rm -rf /tmp/db-backup
      Replace ACTUAL_PASSWORD with natacha password
 7-Build

  Checklist
 1-Confirm you can SSH into ststor01 manually:
  ssh natasha@ststor01
 2-Run the job once manually (Build Now) and check:
  ls -lh /home/natasha/db_backups/
   You should see db_YYYY-MM-DD.sql.
 3-Verify Jenkins console output shows successful dump and transfer.

